-- title:
--   Local index of a product of maximal orders is a square
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda,\Lambda'$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, each assumed to be a maximal order in the sense of the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L63): $\Lambda$ contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, and every submodule with these four properties that contains $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$; likewise for $\Lambda'$. Let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. For a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $M$, write $M_v$ for [`Submodule.localBox M v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in M$ and $c$ in the valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$ of the completion. Then the relative index of $\Lambda_v$ in $(\Lambda\Lambda')_v$, that is the index of $\Lambda_v\cap(\Lambda\Lambda')_v$ in $(\Lambda\Lambda')_v$, where $\Lambda\Lambda'$ denotes the submodule product, equals the square of the relative index of $\Lambda_v\cap\Lambda'_v$ in $\Lambda_v$, i.e. of the index of $\Lambda_v\cap\Lambda'_v$ inside $\Lambda_v$.
--
--   This is the local form, at a single finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$, of the classical relation $[\Lambda\Lambda':\Lambda]=[\Lambda:\Lambda\cap\Lambda']^2$ between two maximal orders of a quaternion algebra. It is used by [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.relIndex_inf_eq_and_relIndex_mul_eq_sq`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.relIndex_inf_eq_and_relIndex_mul_eq_sq), which assembles the local indices into the corresponding global statement.
